    <item>
      <title>Legacy Tyk Pro Helm Chart </title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/tyk-self-managed/tyk-helm-chart/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 01 Jul 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/tyk-self-managed/tyk-helm-chart/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;warning warning-success&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tyk-pro&lt;/code&gt; chart is deprecated. Please use our &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/product-stack/tyk-charts/tyk-stack-chart/&#34;&gt;Tyk Stack helm chart&lt;/a&gt; instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We recommend all users migrate to the &lt;code&gt;tyk-stack&lt;/code&gt; Chart. Please review the &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/product-stack/tyk-charts/tyk-stack-chart/&#34;&gt;Configuration&lt;/a&gt; section of the new helm chart and cross-check with your existing configurations while planning for migration.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;style&gt;&#xA;   &#xA;.warning {&#xA;  padding-top: 0px;&#xA;  padding-left: 20px;&#xA;  padding-right: 20px;&#xA;  background-color: #ffffff;&#xA;  border: 2px solid #FF6C7D;&#xA;  border-radius: 25px;&#xA;  color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&#xA;  font-size: 16px;&#xA;  font-family: &#39;smoolthan&#39;;&#xA;  margin-bottom: 20px;&#xA;}&#xA;.warning strong::after {&#xA;  content: url(&#39;/docs/img/alert.png&#39;);&#xA;  padding-left: 5px;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tyk Helm chart is the preferred (and easiest) way to install &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Self-Managed&lt;/strong&gt; on Kubernetes.&#xA;The helm chart &lt;code&gt;tyk-helm/tyk-pro&lt;/code&gt; will install full Tyk platform with &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Gateways&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Pump&lt;/strong&gt; into your Kubernetes cluster. You can also choose to enable the installation of &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Operator&lt;/strong&gt; (to manage your APIs in a declarative way).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Installation Options for Tyk Self-Managed</title>
